row(15, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE TORAH FOR HIM WHO ACTS IN ERROR. "{H(15, 29, "האזרח", "בבני", "ישראל", "ולגר", "הגר", "בתוכם")}" ("the native-born among the children of Israel and the stranger who sojourns among them") → {A(15, 29, "יציבא", "בבני", "ישראל", "ולגיורא", "דיתגיר", "ביניהון")}; "{H(15, 29, "תורה", "אחת", "יהיה", "לכם", "לעשה", "בשגגה")}" ("one Torah shall be for you for him who does in error" — the third "one Torah"; "for him who does" spelled defective, the Torah\'s one such token; the parser reads 1; computed) → {A(15, 29, "אוריתא", "חדא", "יהי", "לכון", "לדיעבד", "בשלו")} ("one Torah shall be for you, for him who acts in error"). The Sifrei 112:1: R. Yehudah b. Beteira\'s paradigm — willful = karet, unwitting = sin-offering, for EVERY such act: Mishnah Keritot 1:2\'s premise on its verse; gentiles bring no offering; "native-born" includes proselytes wherever written (Lev 23:42\'s sukkah).')
